From 9438684732c0261f2e0eaadffdb9573865b4c3f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:12:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 46/88] xhttp: add the client of Xray's XHTTP transport (work
 in progress)

Client only, after Xray-core v26.9.9 transport/internet/splithttp: modes
packet-up, stream-up and stream-one (auto as Xray: REALITY picks
stream-one, or stream-up with download), HTTP/1.1, 2 and 3 by Xray's ALPN
rule, padding and its obfuscation placements, session ID and sequence
placements, packet-up data in headers or cookies, the XMUX connection pool
and a separate download leg. Option names follow sing-box-extended.

Values Xray refuses or panics on are configuration errors. A dial returns
once the download has a connection, requests run on the session context,
a failed request releases a blocked write, HTTP/2 error types do not leave
the connection, a closed session is not a server failure, and connections
that fail young back new ones off.
